## 1. Definitions

"Software" means the official mau project, including the mau runtime, compiler, command-line tools, editor-support material distributed as part of the project, documentation, examples, configuration, scripts, and other original project material.

"Runtime" means the mau files or portions of mau that are required for a program built with mau to execute.

"Compiler" means the mau compiler and associated command-line tooling that converts `.mau` source files into generated code.

"Generated Output" means code or other files produced by the Compiler from source material supplied by a user.

"Your Product" means software, a website, application, service, game, user interface, commercial product, or other work created using mau that has an independent purpose beyond providing, repackaging, replacing, or reselling mau itself.

"Modified Version" means any fork, adaptation, modification, derivative work, custom build, or other modified version of any part of the Software.

"Distribution" means giving, transmitting, publishing, providing, or otherwise making a copy of the Software or a Modified Version available to another person or entity.

Merely running the Software on infrastructure controlled by you or your organization, without giving another person a copy of the Software, is not Distribution.

"Software Monetization" means charging or receiving payment specifically for the right to obtain, download, license, access, use, or receive the Software or a Modified Version where mau itself, or a substantially equivalent Modified Version, is the product or a primary product being sold.

"Licensor" means HexedMaya with respect to the original mau material owned by HexedMaya.

Rights in Contributions created by other contributors remain subject to the rights held and granted by those contributors.

"Mau Attribution Notice" means a non-user-facing notice identifying mau as the technology that generated or provides part of the relevant code, such as:

"Generated by mau"

or:

"Built with mau"

or equivalent wording produced or approved by the official mau project.

