## 4. Generated Output

Your original source code remains yours.

This License does not claim ownership of original code, text, designs, assets, business logic, or other material that you create merely because that material is processed by mau.

To the extent Generated Output contains material generated from or necessarily incorporating portions of mau, you are granted the rights necessary to use, modify, bundle, deploy, distribute, license, and commercially exploit that Generated Output as part of Your Product.

Generated Output may be:

* modified;
* minified;
* bundled;
* transpiled;
* optimized;
* combined with other software;
* distributed under the license chosen for Your Product;

provided that doing so does not amount to distributing mau itself as a separately reusable framework or software product contrary to this License.

Using Generated Output does not require Your Product to use the mau License.

## 5. Runtime Distribution With Your Product

You may distribute unmodified Runtime components with Your Product where they are reasonably required for Your Product to operate.

This is permitted even when Your Product is sold commercially.

The Runtime may be:

* copied into Your Product;
* delivered to browsers or client devices;
* bundled with Your Product;
* minified or bundled as part of ordinary production builds;
* hosted as part of Your Product.

When distributing Runtime components, you must preserve or reasonably reproduce the applicable mau copyright and license attribution.

This may be provided in:

* the distributed source files;
* a license or notices file;
* package metadata;
* application legal notices;
* documentation;
* another reasonably accessible location accompanying Your Product.

You do not have to display a mau notice prominently to ordinary end users.

Distribution of Runtime components as a necessary part of Your Product does not constitute prohibited Software Monetization.

## 6. Software Monetization Is Prohibited

You may not charge for mau itself or for rights granted by this License.

Without prior written permission from the Licensor, you may not:

* sell copies of mau;
* sell licenses for mau;
* charge for downloading mau;
* rent or lease mau as a software product;
* sell a Modified Version of mau;
* sell licenses for a fork of mau;
* charge for downloading a fork of mau;
* put mau itself behind paid access;
* require a subscription whose primary product is access to mau;
* sell a renamed or rebranded copy of mau;
* sell access to a hosted version whose primary purpose is providing mau itself;
* charge to unlock functionality that belongs to mau itself;
* charge for otherwise restricted mau builds or releases;
* require payment to obtain source code that this License requires to be public.

The substance of an arrangement controls, not the name given to it.

Calling mau "free", "included", "open", "bonus software", or similar wording does not make an arrangement compliant if payment is in substance being required for mau itself.

## 7. Developer Products and Bundles

You may sell developer tools, products, libraries, services, or other material created using mau where that material has substantial independent value and mau is merely a tool or component.

You may not use bundling to sell mau itself.

In particular, you may not sell a framework, SDK, starter kit, boilerplate package, template package, component library, UI kit, development kit, theme package, or similar developer product where mau or a substantially equivalent Modified Version is a material part of the product being sold and the product effectively provides paid access to mau.

A product is not prohibited merely because developers use it or because it interoperates with mau.

The relevant question is whether mau itself is being sold or whether mau is merely being used to create or support an independently valuable product.

